Here's a TypeScript API design prioritizing both clarity (helpfulness) and comprehensive feature coverage (verbosity) for controlling 3D camera animations:

**Core Concepts & Structure**

1. **`CameraController` Class:**  The central hub, managing all animation aspects. Instances represent individual cameras.

   ```typescript
   class CameraController {
       private _target: THREE.Object3D; // Object the camera orbits/tracks
       private _animationDuration: number; // Default:  ms (configurable)
       private _easingFunction: (t: number) => number; //  Easing options (linear, easeInOutQuad, etc.)
